	"dpkg-dev" [label="dpkg-dev" "binary:Synopsis"="Debian package development tools" Breaks="[[{\"name\": \"debhelper\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"10.10.1~\"}], [{\"name\": \"debian-keyring\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"2025.04.25~\"}], [{\"name\": \"devuan-keyring\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"2025.07.30~\"}], [{\"name\": \"gosop\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"1.1.0~\"}], [{\"name\": \"libsop-java-java\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"4.0.7~\"}], [{\"name\": \"pgpainless-cli\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"1.3.13~\"}], [{\"name\": \"rsop\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"0.4.0~\"}], [{\"name\": \"sq\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"0.40.0~\"}], [{\"name\": \"sqop\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"0.27.2~\"}], [{\"name\": \"sqv\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"1.3.0~\"}]]" Description="Debian package development tools
 This package provides the development tools (including dpkg-source)
 required to unpack, build and upload Debian source packages.
 .
 Most Debian source packages will require additional tools to build;
 for example, most packages need make and the C compiler gcc." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=1767 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[[{\"name\": \"dpkg-build-api\", \"op\": \"=\", \"version\": \"0\"}], [{\"name\": \"dpkg-build-api\", \"op\": \"=\", \"version\": \"1\"}]]" Recommends="[[{\"name\": \"build-essential\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"gcc\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"c-compiler\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"fakeroot\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"gnupg\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"sq\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"sqop\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"rsop\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"gosop\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"pgpainless-cli\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"gpg-sq\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"gpgv\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"sqv\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"sqopv\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"rsopv\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"sopv\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"gosop\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"pgpainless-cli\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"gpgv-sq\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"libalgorithm-merge-perl\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Replaces="[]" Section=utils "source:Package"=dpkg "source:Version"="1.23.7ubuntu1" Suggests="[[{\"name\": \"debian-keyring\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"debian-tag2upload-keyring\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Version="1.23.7ubuntu1"]
	e2fsprogs [label=e2fsprogs "binary:Synopsis"="ext2/ext3/ext4 file system utilities" Breaks="[]" Description="ext2/ext3/ext4 file system utilities
 The ext2, ext3 and ext4 file systems are successors of the original ext
 (\"extended\") file system. They are the main file system types used for
 hard disks on Debian and other Linux systems.
 .
 This package contains programs for creating, checking, and maintaining
 ext2/3/4-based file systems.  It also includes the \"badblocks\" program,
 which can be used to scan for bad blocks on a disk or other storage device." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=1530 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[[{\"name\": \"e2fsprogs-l10n\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Replaces="[]" Section=admin "source:Package"=e2fsprogs "source:Version"="1.47.2-3ubuntu4" Suggests="[[{\"name\": \"gpart\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"parted\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"fuse2fs\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"e2fsck-static\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"libarchive13t64\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Version="1.47.2-3ubuntu4"]
	eatmydata [label=eatmydata "binary:Synopsis"="Library and utilities designed to disable fsync and friends" Breaks="[]" Description="Library and utilities designed to disable fsync and friends
 This package contains a small LD_PRELOAD library (libeatmydata) and a couple
 of helper utilities designed to transparently disable fsync and friends (like
 open(O_SYNC)). This has two side-effects: making software that writes data
 safely to disk a lot quicker and making this software no longer crash safe.
 .
 You will find eatmydata useful if particular software calls fsync(), sync()
 etc. frequently but the data it stores is not that valuable to you and you may
 afford losing it in case of system crash. Data-to-disk synchronization calls
 are typically very slow on modern file systems and their extensive usage might
 slow down software significantly. It does not make sense to accept such a hit
 in performance if data being manipulated is not very important.
 .
 On the other hand, do not use eatmydata when you care about what software
 stores or it manipulates important components of your system. The library is
 called libEAT-MY-DATA for a reason." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=21 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=utils "source:Package"=libeatmydata "source:Version"="131-2build1" Suggests="[]" Version="131-2build1"]
	ed [label=ed "binary:Synopsis"="classic UNIX line editor" Breaks="[]" Description="classic UNIX line editor
 ed is a line-oriented text editor.  It is used to
 create, display, modify and otherwise manipulate text
 files.
 .
 red is a restricted ed: it can only edit files in the
 current directory and cannot execute shell commands." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=113 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=editors "source:Package"=ed "source:Version"="1.22.4-1" Suggests="[]" Version="1.22.4-1"]
	eject [label=eject "binary:Synopsis"="ejects CDs and operates CD-Changers under Linux" Breaks="[]" Description="ejects CDs and operates CD-Changers under Linux
 This program will eject CD-ROMs (assuming your drive supports the CDROMEJECT
 ioctl). It also allows setting the autoeject feature.
 .
 On supported ATAPI/IDE multi-disc CD-ROM changers, it allows changing
 the active disc.
 .
 You can also use eject to properly disconnect external mass-storage
 devices like digital cameras or portable music players." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=102 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=utils "source:Package"="util-linux" "source:Version"="2.41.3-3ubuntu2" Suggests="[]" Version="2.41.3-3ubuntu2"]
	ethtool [label=ethtool "binary:Synopsis"="display or change Ethernet device settings" Breaks="[]" Description="display or change Ethernet device settings
 ethtool can be used to query and change settings such as speed, auto-
 negotiation and checksum offload on many network devices, especially
 Ethernet devices." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=1080 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=net "source:Package"=ethtool "source:Version"="1:6.19-1" Suggests="[]" Version="1:6.19-1"]
	fakeroot [label=fakeroot "binary:Synopsis"="tool for simulating superuser privileges" Breaks="[]" Description="tool for simulating superuser privileges
 fakeroot provides a fake \"root environment\" by means of LD_PRELOAD and
 SysV IPC (or TCP) trickery. It puts wrappers around getuid(), chown(),
 stat(), and other file-manipulation functions, so that unprivileged
 users can (for instance) populate .deb archives with root-owned files;
 various build tools use fakeroot for this by default.
 .
 This package contains fakeroot command and the daemon that remembers
 fake ownership/permissions of files manipulated by fakeroot
 processes." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=221 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=utils "source:Package"=fakeroot "source:Version"="1.37.2-1" Suggests="[]" Version="1.37.2-1"]
	fdisk [label=fdisk "binary:Synopsis"="collection of partitioning utilities" Breaks="[]" Description="collection of partitioning utilities
 This package contains the classic fdisk, sfdisk and cfdisk partitioning
 utilities from the util-linux suite.
 .
 The utilities included in this package allow you to partition
 your hard disk. The utilities supports both modern and legacy
 partition tables (eg. GPT, MBR, etc).
 .
 The fdisk utility is the classical text-mode utility.
 The cfdisk utility gives a more userfriendly curses based interface.
 The sfdisk utility is mostly for automation and scripting uses." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=401 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[[{\"name\": \"sensible-utils\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Replaces="[]" Section=utils "source:Package"="util-linux" "source:Version"="2.41.3-3ubuntu2" Suggests="[]" Version="2.41.3-3ubuntu2"]
	file [label=file "binary:Synopsis"="Recognize the type of data in a file using \"magic\" numbers" Breaks="[[{\"name\": \"debhelper\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"12.2~\"}]]" Description="Recognize the type of data in a file using \"magic\" numbers
 The file command is \"a file type guesser\", a command-line tool that
