	"krb5-locales" [label="krb5-locales" "binary:Synopsis"="internationalization support for MIT Kerberos" Breaks="[]" Description="internationalization support for MIT Kerberos
 Kerberos is a system for authenticating users and services on a network.
 Kerberos is a trusted third-party service.  That means that there is a
 third party (the Kerberos server) that is trusted by all the entities on
 the network (users and services, usually called \"principals\").
 .
 This is the MIT reference implementation of Kerberos V5.
 .
 This package contains internationalized messages for MIT Kerberos." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=104 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=localization "source:Package"=krb5 "source:Version"="1.22.1-2ubuntu4" Suggests="[]" Version="1.22.1-2ubuntu4"]
