	"libdeflate0:amd64" [label="libdeflate0:amd64" "binary:Synopsis"="fast, whole-buffer DEFLATE-based compression and decompression" Breaks="[]" Description="fast, whole-buffer DEFLATE-based compression and decompression
 The supported formats are:
  * DEFLATE (raw)
  * zlib (a.k.a. DEFLATE with a zlib wrapper)
  * gzip (a.k.a. DEFLATE with a gzip wrapper)
 .
 libdeflate is heavily optimized. It is significantly faster than the zlib
 library, both for compression and decompression, and especially on x86
 processors. In addition, libdeflate provides optional high compression modes
 that provide a better compression ratio than the zlib's \"level 9\"." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=107 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=libs "source:Package"=libdeflate "source:Version"="1.23-2ubuntu1" Suggests="[]" Version="1.23-2ubuntu1"]
	"libdevmapper1.02.1:amd64" [label="libdevmapper1.02.1:amd64" "binary:Synopsis"="Linux Kernel Device Mapper userspace library" Breaks="[]" Description="Linux Kernel Device Mapper userspace library
 The Linux Kernel Device Mapper is the LVM (Linux Logical Volume Management)
 Team's implementation of a minimalistic kernel-space driver that handles
 volume management, while keeping knowledge of the underlying device layout
 in user-space.  This makes it useful for not only LVM, but software raid,
 and other drivers that create \"virtual\" block devices.
 .
 This package contains the (user-space) shared library for accessing the
 device-mapper; it allows usage of the device-mapper through a clean,
 consistent interface (as opposed to through kernel ioctls)." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=484 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[[{\"name\": \"dmsetup\", \"op\": \">=\", \"version\": \"2:1.02.205-2ubuntu3~\"}]]" Replaces="[]" Section=libs "source:Package"=lvm2 "source:Version"="2.03.31-2ubuntu3" Suggests="[]" Version="2:1.02.205-2ubuntu3"]
