	"libmpc3:amd64" [label="libmpc3:amd64" "binary:Synopsis"="multiple precision complex floating-point library" Breaks="[]" Description="multiple precision complex floating-point library
 MPC is a portable library written in C for arbitrary precision
 arithmetic on complex numbers providing correct rounding. For the time
 being, it contains all arithmetic operations over complex numbers, the
 exponential and the logarithm functions, the trigonometric and
 hyperbolic functions.
 .
 Ultimately, it should implement a multiprecision equivalent of the ISO
 C99 standard.
 .
 It builds upon the GNU MP and the MPFR libraries." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=149 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=libs "source:Package"=mpclib3 "source:Version"="1.3.1-3" Suggests="[]" Version="1.3.1-3"]
	"libmpfr6:amd64" [label="libmpfr6:amd64" "binary:Synopsis"="multiple precision floating-point computation" Breaks="[[{\"name\": \"libgmp3\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"4.1.4-3\"}], [{\"name\": \"libmpc3\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"1.1.0-1~\"}]]" Description="multiple precision floating-point computation
 MPFR provides a library for multiple-precision floating-point computation
 with correct rounding.  The computation is both efficient and has a
 well-defined semantics. It copies the good ideas from the
 ANSI/IEEE-754 standard for double-precision floating-point arithmetic
 (53-bit mantissa)." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=1215 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=libs "source:Package"=mpfr4 "source:Version"="4.2.2-3" Suggests="[]" Version="4.2.2-3"]
