 be specified." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=652 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=libs "source:Package"=libonig "source:Version"="6.9.10-1build1" Suggests="[]" Version="6.9.10-1build1"]
	"libp11-kit0:amd64" [label="libp11-kit0:amd64" "binary:Synopsis"="library for loading and coordinating access to PKCS#11 modules - runtime" Breaks="[]" Description="library for loading and coordinating access to PKCS#11 modules - runtime
 The p11-kit library provides a way to load and enumerate Public-Key
 Cryptography Standard #11 modules, along with a standard configuration
 setup for installing PKCS#11 modules so that they're discoverable. It
 also solves problems with coordinating the use of PKCS#11 by different
 components or libraries living in the same process.
 .
 This package contains the shared library required for applications loading
 and accessing PKCS#11 modules." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=1931 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=libs "source:Package"="p11-kit" "source:Version"="0.26.2-2" Suggests="[]" Version="0.26.2-2"]
	"libpackagekit-glib2-18:amd64" [label="libpackagekit-glib2-18:amd64" "binary:Synopsis"="Library for accessing PackageKit using GLib" Breaks="[]" Description="Library for accessing PackageKit using GLib
 PackageKit allows performing simple software management tasks over a DBus
 interface e.g. refreshing the cache, updating, installing and removing
 software packages or searching for multimedia codecs and file handlers.
 .
 This package provides an advanced library to access PackageKit using GLib.
 It makes use of only async D-Bus calls and provides high level tasks which
 peform the \"transaction dance\"." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=437 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=libs "source:Package"=packagekit "source:Version"="1.3.4-3ubuntu1" Suggests="[]" Version="1.3.4-3ubuntu1"]
	"libpam-cap:amd64" [label="libpam-cap:amd64" "binary:Synopsis"="POSIX 1003.1e capabilities (PAM module)" Breaks="[[{\"name\": \"libcap2-bin\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"1:2.66-1\"}]]" Description="POSIX 1003.1e capabilities (PAM module)
 Libcap implements the user-space interfaces to the POSIX 1003.1e capabilities
 available in Linux kernels. These capabilities are a partitioning of the all
 powerful root privilege into a set of distinct privileges.
 .
 This package contains the PAM module for enforcing capabilities on users and
 groups at PAM session start time." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=56 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[[{\"name\": \"libcap2-bin\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"1:2.66-1\"}]]" Section=admin "source:Package"=libcap2 "source:Version"="1:2.75-10ubuntu2" Suggests="[]" Version="1:2.75-10ubuntu2"]
