	make [label=make "binary:Synopsis"="utility for directing compilation" Breaks="[]" Description="utility for directing compilation
 GNU Make is a utility which controls the generation of executables
 and other target files of a program from the program's source
 files. It determines automatically which pieces of a large program
 need to be (re)created, and issues the commands to (re)create
 them. Make can be used to organize any task in which targets (files)
 are to be automatically updated based on input files whenever the
 corresponding input is newer --- it is not limited to building
 computer programs. Indeed, Make is a general purpose dependency
 solver." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=440 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[[{\"name\": \"make-guile\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Section=devel "source:Package"="make-dfsg" "source:Version"="4.4.1-3" Suggests="[[{\"name\": \"make-doc\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Version="4.4.1-3"]
	"man-db" [label="man-db" "binary:Synopsis"="tools for reading manual pages" Breaks="[]" Description="tools for reading manual pages
 This package provides the man command, the primary way of examining the
 system help files (manual pages). Other utilities provided include the
 whatis and apropos commands for searching the manual page database, the
