	"python-is-python3" [label="python-is-python3" "binary:Synopsis"="symlinks /usr/bin/python to python3" Breaks="[[{\"name\": \"python\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"python-dev-is-python2\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"python-dev-is-python3\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"3.11.1-2\"}], [{\"name\": \"python-is-python2\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"python-is-python2-but-deprecated\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"python-minimal\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Description="symlinks /usr/bin/python to python3
 Starting with the Debian 11 (bullseye) and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS (focal)
 releases, all python packages use explicit python3 or python2
 interpreter and do not use unversioned /usr/bin/python at all. Some
 third-party code is now predominantly python3 based, yet may use
 /usr/bin/python.
 .
 This is a convenience package which ships a symlink to point
 the /usr/bin/python interpreter at the current default python3. It may
 improve compatibility with other modern systems, whilst breaking some
 obsolete or 3rd-party software.
 .
 No packages may declare dependencies on this package." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=16 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[[{\"name\": \"python\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"python-dev-is-python2\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"python-dev-is-python3\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"3.11.1-2\"}], [{\"name\": \"python-is-python2\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"python-is-python2-but-deprecated\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"python-minimal\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Section=python "source:Package"="what-is-python" "source:Version"="15+build1" Suggests="[]" Version="3.13.3-1+build1"]
