	"squashfs-tools" [label="squashfs-tools" "binary:Synopsis"="Tool to create and append to squashfs filesystems" Breaks="[]" Description="Tool to create and append to squashfs filesystems
 Squashfs is a highly compressed read-only filesystem for Linux. It uses zlib
 compression to compress both files, inodes and directories. Inodes in the
 system are very small and all blocks are packed to minimise data overhead.
 Block sizes greater than 4K are supported up to a maximum of 64K.
 .
 Squashfs is intended for general read-only filesystem use, for archival use
 (i.e. in cases where a .tar.gz file may be used), and in constrained block
 device/memory systems (e.g. embedded systems) where low overhead is needed." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=599 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[]" Section=kernel "source:Package"="squashfs-tools" "source:Version"="1:4.7.5-1" Suggests="[]" Version="1:4.7.5-1"]
	sudo [label=sudo "binary:Synopsis"="Provide limited super user privileges to specific users" Breaks="[]" Description="Provide limited super user privileges to specific users
 Sudo is a program designed to allow a sysadmin to give limited root
 privileges to users and log root activity.  The basic philosophy is to give
 as few privileges as possible but still allow people to get their work done." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=3472 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[[{\"name\": \"sudo-rs\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Replaces="[[{\"name\": \"sudo-ldap\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Section=admin "source:Package"=sudo "source:Version"="1.9.17p2-1ubuntu3" Suggests="[]" Version="1.9.17p2-1ubuntu3"]
