 This package provides /etc/sudoers and any other files necessary
 to configure PAM. This package may be used with one of the providers of
 sudo in Ubuntu. Generally this package will be installed as part of
 installing some sudo provider." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=26 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[]" Replaces="[[{\"name\": \"sudo\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"1.9.17p2-1ubuntu2~\"}]]" Section=utils "source:Package"="sudo-common" "source:Version"="1.2ubuntu" Suggests="[]" Version="1.2ubuntu"]
	"sudo-rs" [label="sudo-rs" "binary:Synopsis"="Rust-based sudo and su implementations" Breaks="[]" Description="Rust-based sudo and su implementations
 sudo-rs is a safety-oriented program designed to provide sudo and su
 functionalities with a focus on memory safety. The primary aim is to offer
 a secure and reliable alternative to traditional sudo, ensuring fewer
 vulnerabilities related to memory management.
 .
 While it aims to be a drop-in replacement for most common sudo use cases,
 there are differences in functionality and design. Users should be aware
 of these differences and consult the project's documentation for specifics." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=2489 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[]" Recommends="[[{\"name\": \"libapparmor1\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Replaces="[]" Section=utils "source:Package"="rust-sudo-rs" "source:Version"="0.2.13-0ubuntu1" Suggests="[]" Version="0.2.13-0ubuntu1"]
	systemd [label=systemd "binary:Synopsis"="system and service manager" Breaks="[[{\"name\": \"dracut-core\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"102-2~\"}], [{\"name\": \"less\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"563\"}], [{\"name\": \"sicherboot\", \"op\": \"<<\", \"version\": \"0.1.6\"}]]" Description="system and service manager
 systemd is a system and service manager for Linux. It provides aggressive
 parallelization capabilities, uses socket and D-Bus activation for starting
 services, offers on-demand starting of daemons, keeps track of processes using
 Linux control groups, maintains mount and automount points and implements an
 elaborate transactional dependency-based service control logic.
 .
 Installing the systemd package will not switch your init system unless you
 boot with init=/lib/systemd/systemd or install systemd-sysv in addition." Enhances="[]" InstalledSizeKB=10996 IsEssential=no Maintainer="Ubuntu Developers <ubuntu-devel-discuss@lists.ubuntu.com>" Origin="" Provides="[[{\"name\": \"systemd-sysusers\", \"op\": \"=\", \"version\": \"259.5-0ubuntu3\"}], [{\"name\": \"systemd-tmpfiles\", \"op\": \"=\", \"version\": \"259.5-0ubuntu3\"}]]" Recommends="[[{\"name\": \"default-dbus-system-bus\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"dbus-system-bus\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"linux-sysctl-defaults\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"login\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"systemd-timesyncd\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}, {\"name\": \"time-daemon\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"systemd-resolved\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"systemd-cryptsetup\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Replaces="[]" Section=admin "source:Package"=systemd "source:Version"="259.5-0ubuntu3" Suggests="[[{\"name\": \"systemd-container\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"systemd-homed\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"systemd-userdbd\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"systemd-boot\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"systemd-repart\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"libtss2-tcti-device0\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}], [{\"name\": \"polkitd\", \"op\": null, \"version\": null}]]" Version="259.5-0ubuntu3"]
